# Ansys Fluent and PyFluent write into the current working directory, so launching a
# solver session from this folder leaves process output in the site root. None of it
# belongs to the published site. Run transcripts and report-definition histories are
# kept with their case, under that case's local-output/ folder.
fluent-*.trn
*-rfile.out
fluent-*-error.log
pyfluent_watchdog.err
cleanup-fluent-*.bat
